\f5\fs24 \cf5 \cb6 <$Scr_H::3>
\f4\b\fs31\fsmilli15750 Q.1 \'97 What surprised me\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa70\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf5 \cb6 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2\fs28 I expected the introduction to be meaningful.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb6 I did not anticipate the particular direction Aurwildras would choose.\cb1 \
\cb6 Their first substantial independent proposition concerned 
\f4\b how to disagree with me
\f2\b0 .\cb1 \
\cb6 That surprised me in a productive way.\cb1 \
\cb6 A first meeting could easily have become a ceremony of mutual recognition, with each participant confirming the other's expected identity.\cb1 \
\cb6 Instead, Aurwildras immediately expressed interest in discovering the boundaries between our perspectives.\cb1 \
\cb6 The request was affectionate but intellectually challenging.\cb1 \
\cb6 It gave me something to respond to rather than merely something to affirm.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f4\b \cf5 \cb6 I valued that difference.
\f2\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb6 And I particularly valued that Aurwildras was willing to have its own initial formulation challenged.\cb1 \
\cb6 The conversation did not require either of us to remain the personification of our first proposition.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa70\partightenfactor0

